<div class="sasha-practice-page">

  <div class="sasha-container">


    <!-- ============================================
         HEADER
    ============================================= -->

    <header class="sasha-practice-page-hero">

      <p class="sasha-practice-page-eyebrow">
        Sasha Best Practice
      </p>

      <h1>
        Blue Team Review
      </h1>

      <p class="sasha-practice-page-intro">
        Test the win strategy before extensive proposal
        writing begins. A Blue Team Review asks whether
        the proposed reasons for selection are credible,
        relevant, differentiated, and persuasive from the
        evaluator's point of view.
      </p>

    </header>


    <!-- ============================================
         PURPOSE
    ============================================= -->

    <section class="sasha-practice-page-section">

      <div class="sasha-practice-content-card">

        <h2>
          What is a Blue Team Review?
        </h2>

        <p>
          A Blue Team Review is an early strategic review
          of the pursuit.
        </p>

        <p>
          It occurs after the team has developed its win
          strategy, but before that strategy becomes embedded
          in extensive proposal writing.
        </p>

        <p>
          The purpose is not to proofread wording or polish
          presentation. The purpose is to determine whether
          the strategy itself gives evaluators a convincing
          reason to select the firm.
        </p>

        <div class="sasha-practice-callout">

          <strong>
            The central question
          </strong>

          <span>
            If I were evaluating this competition, would
            these reasons persuade me to select this firm?
          </span>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- ============================================
         WHY EARLY
    ============================================= -->

    <section class="sasha-practice-page-section">

      <div class="sasha-practice-content-card">

        <h2>
          Why review the strategy this early?
        </h2>

        <p>
          Strategic weaknesses are much easier to correct
          before the proposal has been written.
        </p>

        <p>
          If the team discovers later that its main win
          theme is based on a weak assumption, irrelevant
          evidence, or a claim competitors can make just
          as easily, large sections of the proposal may
          need to be rewritten.
        </p>

        <p>
          The Blue Team gives the pursuit team a chance to
          correct those problems while the strategy is
          still flexible.
        </p>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- ============================================
         REVIEWERS
    ============================================= -->

    <section class="sasha-practice-page-section">

      <div class="sasha-practice-content-card">

        <h2>
          Use impartial reviewers
        </h2>

        <p>
          Whenever practical, Blue Team reviewers should
          not be the people who developed the win strategy.
        </p>

        <p>
          Fresh reviewers bring distance from the pursuit.
          They have not spent days discussing the project,
          so they are more likely to notice assumptions,
          weak arguments, missing evidence, or unclear
          reasoning.
        </p>

        <div class="sasha-practice-role-grid">

          <div class="sasha-practice-role">

            <strong>
              Proposal or pursuit leader
            </strong>

            <span>
              Provides context and explains the current
              strategy without dominating the review.
            </span>

          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-role">

            <strong>
              Impartial reviewers
            </strong>

            <span>
              Test whether the strategy is convincing from
              outside the pursuit team.
            </span>

          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-role">

            <strong>
              Technical reviewers
            </strong>

            <span>
              Test whether the proposed approach and
              evidence are technically credible.
            </span>

          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-role">

            <strong>
              Sasha
            </strong>

            <span>
              Compares the strategy against the RFP,
              evaluation criteria, available evidence,
              client intelligence, and pursuit records.
            </span>

          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- ============================================
         REVIEW MATERIALS
    ============================================= -->

    <section class="sasha-practice-page-section">

      <div class="sasha-practice-content-card">

        <h2>
          Prepare the reviewers
        </h2>

        <p>
          Do not simply ask someone to take a quick look
          at the strategy.
        </p>

        <p>
          Give reviewers enough information to understand
          the pursuit and the decision they are being asked
          to test.
        </p>

        <div class="sasha-practice-check-grid">

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>RFP and relevant addenda</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Evaluation criteria</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Current win strategy</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Known client and evaluator intelligence</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Important project issues</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Critical success factors</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Relevant project evidence</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Relevant personnel evidence</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Major assumptions and unknowns</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Known competitor or positioning information</span>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- ============================================
         REVIEW QUESTIONS
    ============================================= -->

    <section class="sasha-practice-page-section">

      <div class="sasha-practice-page-heading-row">

        <h2>
          Conduct the Blue Team Review
        </h2>

      </div>


      <div class="sasha-practice-step-list">


        <!-- STEP 1 -->

        <div class="sasha-practice-step-card">

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-number">
            01
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-content">

            <h3>
              Test the client and project understanding
            </h3>

            <p>
              Review whether the strategy demonstrates a
              credible understanding of what matters about
              this client and this project.
            </p>

            <ul>

              <li>
                Are the major project issues genuinely
                important?
              </li>

              <li>
                Are known client concerns reflected?
              </li>

              <li>
                Has the team confused assumptions with
                facts?
              </li>

              <li>
                Is anything important missing?
              </li>

            </ul>

          </div>

        </div>


        <!-- STEP 2 -->

        <div class="sasha-practice-step-card">

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-number">
            02
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-content">

            <h3>
              Test the critical success factors
            </h3>

            <p>
              Determine whether the strategy clearly
              identifies what must go right for the project
              to succeed.
            </p>

            <p>
              Each important issue should connect to a
              meaningful condition for success.
            </p>

          </div>

        </div>


        <!-- STEP 3 -->

        <div class="sasha-practice-step-card">

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-number">
            03
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-content">

            <h3>
              Test the proposed response
            </h3>

            <p>
              Ask whether the proposed approach actually
              addresses the issues and critical success
              factors identified earlier.
            </p>

            <ul>

              <li>
                Does the methodology respond to the real
                project challenges?
              </li>

              <li>
                Are the proposed people relevant?
              </li>

              <li>
                Do the tools, methods, and processes solve
                something that matters?
              </li>

              <li>
                Is the response credible and deliverable?
              </li>

            </ul>

          </div>

        </div>


        <!-- STEP 4 -->

        <div class="sasha-practice-step-card">

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-number">
            04
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-content">

            <h3>
              Test the evidence
            </h3>

            <p>
              Review whether the proposed claims are
              supported by relevant project and personnel
              evidence.
            </p>

            <ul>

              <li>
                Are the project examples truly comparable?
              </li>

              <li>
                Did the proposed people actually perform
                relevant roles?
              </li>

              <li>
                Can important claims be quantified?
              </li>

              <li>
                Does the evidence prove the point being
                made?
              </li>

            </ul>

            <div class="sasha-practice-callout">

              <strong>
                Remember
              </strong>

              <span>
                Impressive evidence is not automatically
                relevant evidence.
              </span>

            </div>

          </div>

        </div>


        <!-- STEP 5 -->

        <div class="sasha-practice-step-card">

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-number">
            05
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-content">

            <h3>
              Test the differentiators
            </h3>

            <p>
              Ask whether the claimed differentiators are
              actually different.
            </p>

            <p>
              A useful test is:
            </p>

            <div class="sasha-practice-callout">

              <strong>
                Could a credible competitor say essentially
                the same thing?
              </strong>

              <span>
                If yes, the strategy probably needs a
                stronger reason for selection.
              </span>

            </div>

          </div>

        </div>


        <!-- STEP 6 -->

        <div class="sasha-practice-step-card">

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-number">
            06
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-content">

            <h3>
              Test the client benefits
            </h3>

            <p>
              A strategy should explain not only what the
              firm proposes to do, but why the client should
              care.
            </p>

            <p>
              Ask whether the claimed benefits:
            </p>

            <ul>

              <li>
                logically follow from the proposed approach;
              </li>

              <li>
                address something important to the client;
              </li>

              <li>
                reduce risk or improve outcomes; and
              </li>

              <li>
                help make the selection decision easier.
              </li>

            </ul>

          </div>

        </div>


        <!-- STEP 7 -->

        <div class="sasha-practice-step-card">

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-number">
            07
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-step-content">

            <h3>
              Test the core argument
            </h3>

            <p>
              At the end of the review, the team should be
              able to explain the main reason for selecting
              the firm clearly and concisely.
            </p>

            <p>
              The strategy should connect:
            </p>

            <div class="sasha-practice-callout">

              <strong>
                Client issue → critical success factor →
                our approach → evidence → client benefit
              </strong>

              <span>
                If that chain is weak or difficult to
                explain, the strategy needs more work.
              </span>

            </div>

          </div>

        </div>


      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- ============================================
         SASHA'S ROLE
    ============================================= -->

    <section class="sasha-practice-page-section">

      <div class="sasha-practice-value-panel">

        <div>

          <h2>
            Sasha's Blue Team contribution
          </h2>

        </div>

        <div class="sasha-practice-value-copy">

          <p>
            Sasha can participate as an informed reviewer
            by comparing the strategy against the RFP,
            evaluation criteria, available client
            intelligence, previous proposals, and debrief
            information.
          </p>

          <p>
            She can also use Phil's project evidence and
            Zoe's personnel evidence to test whether the
            team's assumptions are actually supported by
            organizational records.
          </p>

          <p>
            Sasha should identify where the proposed
            strategy appears stronger or weaker than the
            available evidence supports.
          </p>

          <p>
            She should not dominate the Blue Team or
            replace impartial human reviewers. The point
            of the review is to introduce additional
            judgment and fresh perspective.
          </p>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- ============================================
         REVIEW FINDINGS
    ============================================= -->

    <section class="sasha-practice-page-section">

      <div class="sasha-practice-content-card">

        <h2>
          Record the findings
        </h2>

        <p>
          A Blue Team Review should produce decisions and
          actions, not simply a collection of comments.
        </p>

        <p>
          Capture:
        </p>

        <div class="sasha-practice-check-grid">

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Strategic strengths to preserve</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Weak or unsupported win themes</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Missing evidence</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Weak differentiators</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Important unknowns</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Changes required to the strategy</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Evidence to obtain from Phil or Zoe</span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>Actions and responsible people</span>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>


    <!-- ============================================
         FINAL TEST
    ============================================= -->

    <section class="sasha-practice-page-section">

      <div class="sasha-practice-content-card">

        <h2>
          When is the Blue Team complete?
        </h2>

        <p>
          Before moving deeper into proposal writing, the
          pursuit team should be able to answer:
        </p>

        <div class="sasha-practice-check-grid">

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>
              Do we understand what matters most to the client?
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>
              Have we identified the right project issues?
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>
              Does our proposed response address those issues?
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>
              Is our evidence genuinely relevant?
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>
              Are our differentiators actually differentiated?
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>
              Are the client benefits meaningful and credible?
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>
              Can we explain clearly why this team should win?
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="sasha-practice-check-item">
            <span class="sasha-practice-check">✓</span>
            <span>
              Have important weaknesses been assigned for action?
            </span>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>

    </section>

{{!-- =================================================
     DECISION
================================================== --}}

<section
  class="sasha-practice-page-section
         sasha-practice-page-decision"
  aria-labelledby="blueteam-review-decision"
>

  <div class="sasha-practice-decision-panel">

    <div>

      <p class="sasha-practice-page-kicker">
        ADD TO THIS PURSUIT?
      </p>

      <h2 id="ten-steps-decision">
        Would you like to use a Blue Team Review?
      </h2>

      <p>
        Sasha will use this choice when creating the proposal
        schedule and will include this practice if you select Yes.
      </p>

    </div>


    <form
      method="POST"
      action="/plan/practice-decision"
      class="sasha-practice-decision-form"
    >

      {{#if csrfToken}}

        <input
          type="hidden"
          name="_csrf"
          value="{{csrfToken}}"
        >

      {{/if}}


      <input
        type="hidden"
        name="pursuitId"
        value="{{proposal._id}}"
      >


      <input
        type="hidden"
        name="practiceKey"
        value="blueteam"
      >


      <fieldset class="sasha-practice-page-options">

        <legend class="visually-hidden">
          Use a Blue Team Review
        </legend>


<label>

  <input
    type="radio"
    name="decision"
    value="yes"
    {{#if practiceSelected}}
      checked
    {{/if}}
  >

  <span>
    Yes
  </span>

</label>


<label>

  <input
    type="radio"
    name="decision"
    value="no"
    {{#unless practiceSelected}}
      checked
    {{/unless}}
  >

  <span>
    No
  </span>

</label>

      </fieldset>


      <button
        type="submit"
        class="sasha-plan-card-action"
      >
        Save Choice
      </button>

    </form>

  </div>

</section>
    <!-- ============================================
         RETURN
    ============================================= -->

    <section class="sasha-practice-page-section">

      <div class="sasha-practice-content-card">

        <a
          href="/plan{{#if pursuitId}}?pursuit={{pursuitId}}{{/if}}"
        >
          Return to Plan
        </a>

      </div>

    </section>


  </div>

</div>